Woodard & Curran is an employee-owned engineering, science, and operations firm dedicated to clean water, a safe environment, healthy communities, and happy people. We foster an inclusive, collaborative culture that supports professional growth, flexibility, and meaningful work, empowering our employees to make a lasting impact on our clients, communities, and the planet.

Woodard & Curran is seeking a dynamic, client-focused SCADA Automation & Controls Engineer to join our team, supporting projects in the Rye Brook, NY area. In this role, you’ll work with municipal and industrial clients on water, wastewater, and remediation projects focused on automation and control systems.

You’ll have the opportunity to work on complex, integrated SCADA solutions, supporting projects from planning and design through implementation and startup. Working alongside project managers, technical managers, engineers, and operations staff, you’ll gain hands-on experience while taking increasing ownership of technical deliverables and client solutions.

This role offers a strong combination of technical growth, autonomy, client impact, and career advancement. You’ll work directly with clients to solve operational challenges, improve system performance, and develop solutions that make a meaningful impact on their operations.

This position involves regular travel to job sites, typically within driving distance, to support project startups, meetings, and client needs.

Who are we looking for:
The successful candidate will join a collaborative team delivering medium-to-large SCADA implementation projects for municipal and industrial water and wastewater clients. Projects may be standalone or part of larger multidisciplinary solutions.

We’re looking for someone with strong technical and communication skills who can effectively manage responsibilities within project scope, schedule, and budget. As your experience grows, you’ll have opportunities to take on greater project ownership, expand your technical expertise, and develop into larger technical and client leadership responsibilities.

Offering Flexible Hybrid work schedule consisting of office, remote, and onsite work based on project needs.

Travel: Regional travel up to 80%. Occasional overnight travel.

What you will be doing at Woodard & Curran
Participate in site investigations to evaluate client systems, equipment, and instrumentation and support project planning and cost estimates;
Develop process logic for Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs) used to monitor and control water and wastewater treatment systems;
Design Human Machine Interface (HMI) and Operator Interface Terminal (OIT) graphical screens;
Develop automated reports to collect and communicate SCADA system data;
Support installation, checkout, and modification of field wiring and control system equipment;
Configure and calibrate instrumentation, including level, pressure, flow, temperature, and process analyzers;
Configure and commission industrial networking hardware, including Ethernet switches, wireless access points, and licensed frequency radios;
Participate in system testing, commissioning, and startup to ensure equipment, instrumentation, and SCADA systems operate as intended;
Train operations personnel on the use, maintenance, and troubleshooting of SCADA hardware and software;
Participate in QA/QC activities for design deliverables and controls programming;
Take increasing ownership of technical deliverables and client solutions as experience grows;
Follow all required safety procedures and protocols.

What you will need to succeed:
BS in Electrical Engineering, Computer Systems Engineering, Industrial Engineering, or a related field;
2-3 years of experience in control system integration;
Experience with Allen-Bradley PLC hardware and software;
Experience with HMI software such as Allen-Bradley FactoryTalk, AVEVA Wonderware, Ignition, or GE Proficy iFIX;
Experience configuring and developing graphics for OITs such as All

Veeam is the Data and AI Trust Company, specializing in helping organizations ensure their data and AI are fully understood, secured, and resilient to enable the acceleration of safe AI at scale. As the market leader in both data resilience and data security posture management, Veeam is built for the convergence of identity, data, security, and AI risk. Headquartered in Seattle with offices in more than 30 countries, Veeam protects over 550,000 customers worldwide, who trust Veeam to keep their businesses running. Join us as we go fearlessly forward together, growing, learning, and making a real impact for some of the world’s biggest brands.

About the Role &nbsp;

We are seeking a Software Development Engineer in Test (SDET) to serve as a principal technical leader across our core platform infrastructure in Bangalore. In this high-impact role, you will define the quality architecture, multi-cloud testing strategies, and automation frameworks for some of our most critical engineering initiatives. &nbsp;

You will own end-to-end quality for high-throughput Connectors (at massive scale) , complex Graph Data Structures , custom Reporting Engines , and on-premise/localized System-Level Testing . You will bridge cloud-native engineering and quality engineering by building production-grade test infrastructure, benchmarking systems across AWS, Azure, and Kubernetes , and setting technical excellence standards across the engineering organization. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities &nbsp;

1. Architecture, Multi-Cloud &amp; K8s Infrastructure Leadership &nbsp;

• Cloud-Native Test Architecture: Design, build, and maintain scalable, extensible test automation frameworks and harnesses across AWS and Azure environments. &nbsp;

• Kubernetes Automation: Architect dynamic, containerized test infrastructure leveraging Kubernetes (K8s) to spin up ephemeral test clusters, mock environments, and end-to-end integration environments on demand. &nbsp;

• Technical Strategy: Drive the overall test and quality strategy across cloud and local topologies, establishing best practices for unit, integration, microservices, chaos, and performance testing. &nbsp;

• CI/CD Pipeline Integration: Integrate automated validation systems into localized and cloud-based Continuous Integration / Continuous Delivery (CI/CD) pipelines (e.g., GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure DevOps). &nbsp;

&nbsp;

2. Domain-Specific Ownership &nbsp;

• Scale Connectors: Build robust testing tools to validate high-volume data connectors, API integrations, and ingestion pipelines across multi-cloud setups ( AWS S3/SQS, Azure Blob/Event Hubs ). Stress test for concurrency, throughput, message loss, network degradation, and cloud cost efficiency at scale. &nbsp;

• Graph Engine &amp; Traversal: Architect test matrices and verification suites for complex Graph databases/architectures (e.g., AWS Neptune, Neo4j, GraphQL ), verifying node-edge relationship queries, indexing performance, and path traversal correctness under heavy concurrent loads. &nbsp;

• Reporting &amp; Analytics: Validate data fidelity, aggregation logic, latency, and correctness across high-volume reporting engines and dynamic query visualization platforms. &nbsp;

• Local System Testing: Drive local environment and system-level integration testing in our San Jose lab/office-ensuring localized hardware/software dependencies, edge topologies, and containerized local Kubernetes environments (e.g., Minikube, K3s, Kind) operate seamlessly under real-world scenarios. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

3. Quality Engineering &amp; Operations &nbsp;

• Identify architectural bottlenecks, reliability risks, and memory leaks before features hit production across AWS, Azure, and local systems. &nbsp;

• Establish standard observability, distributed tracing (e.g., Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog), and automated reporting dashboards to expose systemic quality issues and pipeline health. &nbsp;

• Code review, mentor, and elevate the technical engineer
